# Docker build context = ALLOWLIST. Only what the Dockerfile copies is sent to
# the builder (locally or Fly's remote builder): no node_modules, dist, .tmp,
# .git, docs, tests or the old site's root files. Add a path here only when
# the Dockerfile starts to COPY it (test/ops.test.js checks both agree).
*
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!scripts/
!src/
!data/
!deploy/

# Never, even inside the allowed directories.
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/*.log
**/.env
**/.env.*
